CORE
s_eventually5.sv
--bound 2
^\[main\.p0\] always \(s_eventually \[3:3\] main\.c == 3\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.p1\] always \(s_eventually \[2:3\] main\.c == 3\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.p2\] always \(s_nexttime\[3\] main\.c == 3\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
s_eventually [a:b] p whose window extends beyond the BMC bound is
inconclusive and must not produce a counterexample.  p0 and p1 have
c==3 holding at t=3, which is beyond --bound 2, so both must be PROVED
up to the bound rather than REFUTED.  s_nexttime[3] (p2) is equivalent
and handled the same way.
